  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196700: Bounded PostgreSQL COPY IN and OUT

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The database provider exposes separate bounded COPY OUT and COPY IN component
operations. COPY responses use a dedicated state machine instead of being
accepted by the ordinary query parser. It validates overall and per-column
formats, a maximum of 64 columns, every message frame, CopyDone,
CommandComplete and the final ReadyForQuery in exact order.

COPY IN accepts at most 4096 bytes from a memory range independent of SQL. The
provider waits for a valid CopyInResponse before emitting exactly one CopyData
frame and one CopyDone frame. Query errors are drained through ReadyForQuery
and returned as typed SQLSTATE metadata so the affine session remains usable.
COPY OUT is bounded by consumer output capacity and rejects incomplete or
conflicting stream terminals.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification creates a temporary int4 table, COPYs
three rows IN, COPYs the ordered rows OUT as three chunks, queries and verifies
sum 6, closes the session and proves no native transport handles remain.

This closes the bounded single-buffer COPY slice. Incremental multi-chunk
stream handles, batch/pipeline execution, pooling, rotation, compatibility
matrices and soak remain open.")))
